# Face model weights. Downloaded and SHA-256 verified by
# services/face-ai/scripts/fetch_models.py, never committed: ~37 MiB of binary,
# and weights whose commercial-use status is still unresolved
# (services/face-ai/app/models/LICENSING.md) do not belong in source control.
services/face-ai/models/
*.onnx

# Python
services/*/.venv/
services/*/__pycache__/
services/*/**/__pycache__/
services/*/*.egg-info/
services/*/.pytest_cache/

# logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# OS
.DS_Store

# editors
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/

# misc
*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo/

# --- Defense-in-depth for public-repository posture ---
#
# The tree does not currently contain any of these paths, but publishing a
# repository is a one-way action and a future `git add .` should not be the
# thing that undoes it. Every rule below either protects a category of
# credential this project could conceivably grow (release signing, TLS
# material, integration secrets) or catches a local-only artefact that has
# already accumulated in the working tree (`.claude/` scratch, personal
# architecture PDFs). Duplicates of rules above are not repeated.
.claude/
*.pdf
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
credentials/
secrets/
local.properties
